{"availability":"available","full":"amyrmahdy/decima","name":"decima","description":"Open, CPU-sized Jev-style (System One) decision model: situation + question + options → calibrated probabilities. 122M, ~20 ms on one CPU core, runs in your browser.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-27T12:12:35Z","updated":"2026-10-04T07:50:45Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["calibration","decision-model","jev","jev-alternative","multilingual","onnx","system-one","typed-decisions","zero-shot-classification"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/amyrmahdy/decima-playground","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:26.156Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:26.156Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:26.156Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:26.156Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Situation + question + your options → calibrated probabilities. Like TypeSafe's Jev, Decima is a System One model: typed decisions with probabilities instead of generated text. Unlike Jev, it is open (Apache-2.0), runs on a CPU, and speaks the same /v1/systemone API.","Built by A. M. Madani (@amyrmahdy · amyrmahdy.github.io). The name: DECIsion MAking — and Decima is also the Roman Fate who decides.","Decima does not write text. It decides: routing, triage, intent, classification, verification, ranking — any bounded choice your software needs to make, with a confidence it can threshold."],"features":["decima-base (mmBERT-base) is a new generation.","decima-agent, fine-tuned from it, is the decision layer for agent loops: 0.90 on 130 hand-written agent decisions","Claude Code hooks run locally, put rules first and fail closed.","A Persian edition of the jabr benchmark.","decima-small: 122M parameters, ONNX int8, 20 ms per decision on one laptop CPU core (4 options, short input)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amyrmahdy/decima/bl